what is the workflow of terraform and How its works ??
=======================================================

In our projects we use Terraform as IAC tool infra structure as a code  
Instead of manually creating the resources like RG, vm, vpn, storage accounts, key-vault, LB, acr, aks 

we can write terraform configuration files to create resources automatically on any cloud platform.

Coming to Terraform workflow
1st thing we need to write .tf files like 
main.tf --- where we write all our entire code in main.tf
provider.tf --- azurerm cloud provider
variables.tf --- variables added
terraform.tfvars -- variables declare
once the .tf files are ready 

1st we need to use 
terraform init --- to downloads the plugins and initialize the working directory and .terraform folder creates
terraform validate -- it will check the code syntax 
terraform fmt -- to make code alignment correct 
terraform plan -- create a plan by comparing the code and state file like current infra vs desire infra
terraform apply -- then resources will create on cloud by provider api 
after resources are created successfully -- then terraform will update the state file for tracking 

and we will store the state file in storage account by remote backend for state locking 

terraform destroy -- it will delete all infra,
 if only particular resource we have to use target= resource name 
this is the workflow and how terraform works !
